# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in what you use. Everything here is optional:
# a feature whose settings are missing shows as "not configured" and the rest works.

# Where the knowledge base lives. Defaults to this repo.
# BRAIN_ROOT=~/Documents
# PORT=5200

# Calendar widget: Google Calendar → Settings → (your calendar) → Integrate calendar →
# "Secret address in iCal format". Several calendars: separate with commas.
CALENDAR_ICS_URLS=
# CALENDAR_REFRESH_MINS=5

# Email widget: a Google Cloud OAuth client (Desktop or Web) with the Gmail read-only scope.
# Add http://localhost:5200/api/gmail/callback as an authorised redirect URI, then sign in
# from the widget. The refresh token is kept in the macOS Keychain, not here.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GMAIL_FEED=0          # turn the email feed off
# EMAIL_REFRESH_SECS=60

# Claude chats: each chat uses a Claude Code sign-in of your own (subscription or API key).
# LAIKA_BRIEFS=0        # stop the one-line chat summaries (they use a small model call)
# LAIKA_BRIEF_MODEL=haiku

# Optional sibling tools
# SHOWREEL_DIR=../laika-showreel
# MISSION_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7317

# Adoption pulse (/pulse): the node network of people arriving and, if they opt in, using the app.
# Public repo numbers need a token with `repo` scope to read GitHub's traffic API. Prefer the
# Keychain: `security add-generic-password -s 'laika-orbit secret' -a pulse-github-token -w`
# PULSE_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# PULSE_REPO=Laika-Dynamics-Ltd/laika-orbit
# Opt-in telemetry. Without PULSE_ENDPOINT the app cannot report at all, whatever the user chose.
# See tools/pulse-ingest/README.md and PRIVACY.md.
# PULSE_ENDPOINT=https://laika-pulse.<subdomain>.workers.dev
# PULSE_READ_TOKEN=
# The /pulse window and its rail button appear only on the operator's machine. Either token above
# is taken as proof of that; PULSE_OPERATOR=1 forces it on, 0 forces it off. It hides the door,
# not the data — a user without the tokens has an empty store to look at.
# PULSE_OPERATOR=
